  "generation": {
    "change_summary": "Added a Suit Dedication mechanic: after the deal, each player simultaneously and secretly selects one suit as their dedicated suit (then all reveal). Playing cards of that suit increments a public dedication count. At game end, each player earns a bonus of 5 points per dedicated-suit card played, which is added to the winner's payoff or subtracted from losers' payments.",
    "mechanic_hypothesis": "By requiring each player to commit to a personal suit identity at game start, every subsequent card play gains personal significance (advancing or failing to advance one's dedication). This creates a coherent personal narrative arc across the entire game, making each decision feel like it contributes to a larger plan rather than being a mere legal move. The System Purist can optimize suit selection based on hand composition and visible play history, and the public dedication count creates a sense of visible personal progress and investment.",
    "unchanged_invariants": [
      "Player count unchanged",
      "Core shedding objective unchanged (empty hand to win)",
      "Turn structure unchanged (one action per turn)",
      "Legal action space unchanged (play matching, play eight, draw, pass)",
      "Information boundaries unchanged (hands hidden, stock hidden, play history public)",
      "Wild eight mechanics unchanged",
      "Stock exhaustion and pass rules unchanged",
      "Base card point values unchanged",
      "Deck composition unchanged (52 cards, no jokers)",
      "Initial deal of 5 cards unchanged"
    ],
    "observable_trace_changes": [
      "A new simultaneous secret selection phase occurs after dealing and before first turn",
      "Each player's dedicated suit becomes public information after reveal",
      "Dedication count is publicly trackable and increments when a player plays a card of their dedicated suit",
      "Players may strategically prefer to play cards of their dedicated suit when multiple legal plays exist",
      "Players may strategically choose their dedicated suit based on initial hand composition",
      "Final payoff calculations include dedication bonus adjustments",
      "Players may voluntarily draw to seek cards of their dedicated suit even when a non-dedicated play is available"
    ],
    "implementation_notes": [
      "The dedication selection is simultaneous and secret (write-down or equivalent) to prevent anchoring on other players' choices",
      "Dedication count is derivable from public play history, so no hidden state is added",
      "The 5-point bonus value is calibrated to be meaningful relative to typical hand values (average remaining hand ~20-40 points) without dominating the base shedding incentive",
      "Eights do not count toward dedication regardless of declared suit, preserving their wild-card identity",
      "The mechanic adds exactly one decision point (suit selection) and one ongoing consideration (prioritizing dedicated suit plays) without altering the action resolution structure"
    ],
    "risk_notes": [
      "If a player's dedicated suit becomes impossible to play (e.g., all cards of that suit are in opponents' hands or stock), the dedication becomes a dead weight—this is an acceptable strategic risk that adds meaning to the initial choice",
      "The bonus could theoretically incentivize holding cards rather than shedding them, but the 5-point bonus per card is small relative to the penalty of holding high-value cards at game end",
      "The simultaneous reveal prevents gaming the system but means players cannot adapt their dedication to the starter card—this is intentional to preserve the commitment feeling",
      "In exhaustion-end scenarios, the dedication bonus could shift the winner from what base hand values would suggest, which is the intended effect of rewarding strategic play"
    ]
  },
